// Which pixels screen-space reflections may write at all. ONE statement, read by the trace (SSR.shader) and by
// the tile classification that decides where the trace, resolve and composite are drawn
// (SSRTileClassify.shader): if the two disagreed, a pixel the trace would reflect could sit in a tile nobody
// draws, and its reflection would silently vanish.

// Rough surfaces reflect too diffusely for a sharp SSR ray, so they fade out early (a soft gate, not a
// metal-only cutoff: a smooth dielectric floor still gets its Fresnel reflection, as in UE).
float SSRSmoothFade(float roughness)
{
	return smoothstep(0.4, 0.7, 1.0 - roughness);
}

// The trace's own early-outs that depend on the G-buffer alone: sky (no normal) or too rough to reflect.
// A pixel failing this is written 0 by the trace.
bool SSRPixelCanReflect(vec4 gbufferNormal)
{
	return dot(gbufferNormal.rgb, gbufferNormal.rgb) > 0.001 && SSRSmoothFade(gbufferNormal.a) >= 0.01;
}
